# Dependency Injection System

Dokan Kits uses a dependency injection container based on League Container for managing services and dependencies.

## Core Container Files

- [includes/Core/DI/Container.php](mdc:includes/Core/DI/Container.php): Extended container implementation
- [includes/Core/DI/Providers/ServiceProvider.php](mdc:includes/Core/DI/Providers/ServiceProvider.php): Main service provider that registers all other providers

## Service Providers

Service providers are responsible for registering services with the container:

- [CoreServiceProvider.php](mdc:includes/Core/DI/Providers/CoreServiceProvider.php): Core services
- [AdminServiceProvider.php](mdc:includes/Core/DI/Providers/AdminServiceProvider.php): Admin-related services
- [RestServiceProvider.php](mdc:includes/Core/DI/Providers/RestServiceProvider.php): REST API controllers
- [FeaturesServiceProvider.php](mdc:includes/Core/DI/Providers/FeaturesServiceProvider.php): Feature classes
- [DataStoreServiceProvider.php](mdc:includes/Core/DI/Providers/DataStoreServiceProvider.php): Data stores

## Using the Container

To access the container or retrieve services:

```php
// Get the container
$container = dokan_kits_get_container();

// Get a service
$service = dokan_kits_service('service-id');

// Or use the helper function for common services
$template_manager = dokan_kits_template_manager();
```

## Adding Custom Services

To extend the container with custom services:

```php
add_action('dokan_kits_register_service_providers', function($provider) {
    $provider->getContainer()->addServiceProvider(new MyCustomServiceProvider());
});
```
